Three changes in three files. No painted element is added or removed, no CSS rule moves and no font size
changes: the section still paints 85 elements open and 10 collapsed, and 10 px is still its smallest
painted font in the open and expanded states (11 px in the collapsed bar, which is the baseline's
own reading). The fixture and the protocol are the baseline's.

Change 1 of 3 - the head names the project and the tree
  what moved: the first fact of the card head's meta line, now built as `whyHomeless` in
    public/render-jobs.js. A card whose cwd is `.worktrees/<name>` reads
    `worktree feat-long-tree-name · beta` where it read `no worktree`; a plain directory keeps
    `no worktree`, and a recorded owner that is not a row keeps `owner <path> (not in the scan)`.
    The same false word was on the card whose tree the board HAS read, so that card now reads
    `worktree feat-one · alpha` too. The head stays 27.75 px and the card 266.17 px tall; only the
    meta span grows (191.34 to 349.69 px on the unread card, 283.70 px on the read one), inside the
    head's own nowrap/ellipsis span.
  asked by: "an unattached card whose cwd is a worktree the board has not read must say where that
    directory actually is" - the first clause of the implement brief's change sentence.

Change 2 of 3 - the picker offers the card's own tree
  what moved: the attach press's on-demand picker build in public/app.js. When the card's cwd is
    `.worktrees/<name>` and the board has no row at that path, the select now gets
    `beta · feat-long-tree-name (not read)` as its first option, with the tree's real path as the
    value, selected; Attach is enabled for it. The disabled `the row for feat-long-tree-name is
    missing` placeholder (value "", selected, Attach disabled) is gone. The three board rows stay
    below it, so the picker is still a picker: measured options 4 to 4, selected index 3 to 0,
    selected text `beta · feat-long-tree-name (not read)`, Attach disabled to enabled. The select is
    intrinsic-width, so replacing the long placeholder narrows it 325 to 268 px and moves the
    49.45 x 21 Attach button from x 449.39 to 392.39; the row keeps its 24 px height and the button
    its size.
  asked by: "its attach picker must offer that card's own tree instead of four other trees and a
    disabled placeholder" - the second clause of the same sentence.

Change 3 of 3 - the press on that tree answers with the tree, not its parent
  what moved: `attachMeaning` in lib/job-trees.js. A press that names the run's own tree is refused
    honestly when the board has no row for it: the 409 used to describe that very tree as "only the
    checkout that contains it" (the parent-row sentence, reached because the asked path equals the
    run's root); it now names the tree, the checkout and the scan root that would give it a row.
    Measured against the baseline fixture: "the row for <sandbox>/fixture/outside/beta/.worktrees/
    feat-long-tree-name is missing - the board reads only the repositories directly inside a scan
    root, and <sandbox>/fixture/outside/beta is not one of them, so it has never read that tree.
    Add <sandbox>/fixture/outside under Settings > Board > Folders the board scans, then reload".
    The press files nothing, as before. A press on the parent checkout keeps the old sentence (and
    the test at test/assistant-queue-reattach.test.js:403 that names it).
  asked by: the same second clause - offering the tree makes its press answerable. The baseline's
    own target states the allowance: "or say plainly that the board has no row for it and what
    would make one".

Which of the baseline's three states the change moves:
  open      moves. The first card's head meta is the changed text (the surface shot differs); the
            section still 1408 x 580.34 px with 85 painted elements, jobs 531.34 px, cards 266.17
            and 265.17 px, smallest font 10 px.
  expanded  moves. The picker's option set and the Attach press (disabled to enabled); the section
            still 1408 x 609.34 px with 89 painted elements and smallest font 10 px.
  collapsed does not move. The bar is untouched, it still paints 10 elements in 48 px, and the
            surface shot's sha256 is identical to the baseline's
            (d3c761fe9345c905e7e6e85aae8e90a5dd88bf9c006e35e9a2e93d23a37c08c6).

Verification of the after state: the baseline's capture.mjs, run against this tree in a throwaway
sandbox with the same fixture and steps, wrote an open card meta of
`worktree feat-long-tree-name · beta · (default model)`, an expanded picker whose first option is
`beta · feat-long-tree-name (not read)` with the tree's path as its value and four enabled options,
and a collapsed surface shot byte-identical to the baseline's. A press on the offered tree was
driven in the same sandbox; the banner quoted under change 3 is its answer. No test/*.test.js file
was run for this stage (the brief forbids it); node --check passes on all three files, and the one
test that names the parent-row sentence is untouched by this change.

